Environment Variables

Create a `.env` file in the root directory.

```env
ATLASDB_URL=your_mongodb_connection_string

SECRET=your_session_secret

MAP_TOKEN=your_mapbox_token

CLOUDINARY_CLOUD_NAME=your_cloudinary_cloud_name
CLOUDINARY_KEY=your_cloudinary_key
CLOUDINARY_SECRET=your_cloudinary_secret
```

Do not upload your `.env` file to GitHub.

---

## Installation & Setup

### 1. Clone the repository

git clone <your-github-repository-url>

2. Navigate into the project

cd Wanderlust

### 3. Install dependencies

npm install

### 4. Create environment variables

Create a `.env` file and add the required credentials.

### 5. Start the application

node app.js

Or, if you have a development script:

npm run dev

### 6. Open in browser

http://localhost:8080


## Authentication & Authorization

Wanderlust uses session-based authentication.

The authentication flow is:

```text
User Login
    ↓
Passport.js
    ↓
Verify Credentials
    ↓
Create Session
    ↓
Session Cookie
    ↓
Authenticated Requests
```

Authorization is used to make sure users can only modify resources they are allowed to manage.

---

## Mapbox Integration

Mapbox is used for location-based functionality.

When a listing is created:

```text
Listing Location
      ↓
Mapbox Geocoding
      ↓
Latitude / Longitude
      ↓
GeoJSON Coordinates
      ↓
MongoDB
      ↓
Map Display
```

This allows listings to be displayed at their corresponding geographic locations.

---

## Cloudinary Integration

Cloudinary is used to store listing images.

The upload flow is:

```text
User
 ↓
Image Upload
 ↓
Multer
 ↓
Cloudinary
 ↓
Image URL
 ↓
MongoDB Listing
```

This keeps image storage separate from the application server.

